    "event": "Special Weather Statement",
    "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
    "senderName": "NWS New Orleans LA",
    "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued November 12 at 10:24AM CST by NWS New Orleans LA",
    "description": "Elevated fire weather conditions can be expected across portions\nof southeast Louisiana and southern Mississippi this afternoon.\nRelative humidity values are forecast to drop into the 25 to 35\npercent range, especially near and north of the Interstate 10 and\n12 corridors. The 20 ft wind forecast is expected to remain at or\nbelow 10 mph in most areas, which should limit critical fire\nweather conditions or at least the effective spread of fires that\nmay ignite.\n\nNumerous local burn bans are in place across LA and MS due to\nongoing drought conditions. Outdoor burning is strongly\ndiscouraged as the ongoing drought conditions continue, and all\nlocal restrictions should be followed.",
    "instruction": null,
    "response": "Execute",
