    "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
    "senderName": "NWS Upton NY",
    "headline": "Marine Weather Statement issued November 12 at 11:16AM EST by NWS Upton NY",
    "description": "The areas affected include...\n\nSandy Hook NJ to Fire Island Inlet NY out 20 NM...\nNew York Harbor...\n\nAt 1116 AM EST, Doppler radar indicated a strong thunderstorm,\ncapable of producing winds to around 30 knots. This thunderstorm was\nlocated over Leonardo, moving north at 15 knots.\n\nThe strong thunderstorm will be near...\nSandy Hook and Sandy Hook Bay around 1120 AM EST.\nLower New York Harbor around 1140 AM EST.",
    "instruction": "Mariners can expect gusty winds to around 30 knots, locally higher\nwaves, lightning strikes, and heavy downpours. Boaters should seek\nsafe harbor immediately until this storm passes.",
